/-
Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Law/Skel/Full/Data.lean: DATA, MADE BY PROGRAM: what the four closed facts of
`ProofFile.Sk.back_of_written` (Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Law/Skel/SkelWritten.lean) read, AT THE FULL SIZE,
as Lean text: the places, the shape, the batchings' places, the segments' sorts, the fifteen lots'
skeletons as plain data, the two later seats' names and stand-ins, the blocks at the places and the
first chain's flat list in skeletons. Definitions alone.
WHENCE. Lean's evaluator has printed these values off the makers themselves (`ProofFile.pubPlain`,
`ProofFile.baseOf`, `ProofFile.Sk.lotW` of each lot's `ProofFile.Sk.lotSk`, `ProofFile.Sk.placesSk`, `ProofFile.Sk.chainBySk`) at
the full-size example's three public files. A program has cut the print, has written each told tree
and each of its tenants as a tuple in angle brackets, in the fields' order (log-length, words,
tenants | main, mask, degree, sampled, groups), and has wrapped the lines at 100 letters, breaking
only behind a comma outside a string. A second run of the evaluator has held the makers' values,
made anew, against this text: the same at all nine values; not the same at thirteen altered ones.
Limits. NOTHING HERE IS PROVED: that these are the makers' values at the public files is what each
lot's row, and the rows on the places, the shape and the sorts, have to show. THE TEXT COMES OFF THE
VERY CODE THAT IT DESCRIBES: it is no independent witness. In a lot's blocks a name is the block's
own; in `baseW` and `flatW` it is the place's. The example's weights are synthetic.

-/
